/**
 * Platform Owner PO-02C (company access: suspend, reactivate and customer enforcement) — the approved change to files the
 * DEV-UI-01.7, ACC-01, LCP, PO-01A, PO-01B, PO-01B.1, PO-02A and PO-02B verifiers freeze.
 *
 * PO-02C is the first platform layer that changes CUSTOMER authentication, and only behind a switch that is off by default
 * (TENANT_ACCESS_ENFORCEMENT=enabled): the session check (src/lib/session.ts), the session store (one read helper), sign-in
 * and session issuance (src/app/(auth)/actions.ts), the signed-file path of the uploads route and the customer dictionary
 * (nine strings) — plus two added customer files, the tenant-access gate (the ONE customer module that consults the access
 * rule) and the access-suspended screen. On the platform side it adds the access action, its server actions and dialog,
 * appends platform.companies.manage_access and the ENFORCEMENT_DISABLED code, reads the company detail's access state in
 * one statement, makes the access notes truthful and gives the console dialog a mobile sheet. No schema, migration,
 * business, accounting, inventory, HR, document, print, payment or API file is in either list.
 *
 * The rule for an approved change is the one C8, ACC-01, the LCP stage and PO-01A…PO-02B used: no re-baseline. Each changed
 * file's hunks are recorded here byte for byte, [7637e4e's text, PO-02C's text]; undone, the file is PO-02B's (7637e4e) to the
 * byte (PO02C_BASE_SHA), so every older pin keeps its strength. The added files are listed with their sha256 (PO02C_NEW) and
 * left out of the older pins' walks. Each freeze verifier's PO-02C check proves the hunks are each file's only change, and
 * verify-page-archetypes group 26 pins the customer deltas line by line.
 *
 * Generated from the diff against PO02C_BASE (each hunk widened with context until it is unique in both files, its 7637e4e
 * form nowhere in PO-02C's); changing a PO-02C file means regenerating this record, which is then part of the change under
 * review.
 */
